<p><code>Pdf::extractAsImages()</code> rasterizes the pages of an existing PDF into standalone image files, one
per page, and returns the paths it wrote. Install the <code>imagick</code> extension with a PDF delegate
before you call it — that extension is what does the rasterizing.</p>
<h2 id="extracting-every-page">Extracting Every Page<a class="anchor" href="#extracting-every-page" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Two arguments — the PDF to read and the directory to write into:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Given a three-page <code>invoice.pdf</code>, that writes <code>invoice-01.jpg</code>, <code>invoice-02.jpg</code> and
<code>invoice-03.jpg</code> into <code>pages/</code> and returns their full paths in an array keyed by 1-based page
number:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code>[
    <span class="text-num">1</span> =&gt; <span class="text-str">&#039;/path/to/pages/invoice-01.jpg&#039;</span>,
    <span class="text-num">2</span> =&gt; <span class="text-str">&#039;/path/to/pages/invoice-02.jpg&#039;</span>,
    <span class="text-num">3</span> =&gt; <span class="text-str">&#039;/path/to/pages/invoice-03.jpg&#039;</span>,
]
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The key is the page number in the source document:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-kw">foreach</span> (<span class="text-var">$images</span> <span class="text-kw">as</span> <span class="text-var">$pageNumber</span> =&gt; <span class="text-var">$image</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$pageNumber</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;: &#039;</span> . <span class="text-fn">basename</span>(<span class="text-var">$image</span>) . <span class="text-str">&quot;\n&quot;</span>;
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The name in front of the page number is the source file's name without its extension, so files
from several PDFs extracted into one directory stay grouped by document. Create the destination
directory before the call and make it writable — the method writes into it rather than creating it.</p>
<p>To know how many files are coming before any are written, <code>Build\Image\Extractor::countPages()</code>
counts a document's pages directly:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Image\Extractor</span>;

<span class="text-var">$extractor</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Extractor</span>();
<span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$extractor</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">countPages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That prints <code>3</code>. Building an <code>Extractor</code> is also the cheapest way to check <code>imagick</code> is present,
since that's where the extension is looked for.</p>
<h2 id="formats-and-resolution">Formats and Resolution<a class="anchor" href="#formats-and-resolution" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>The third and fourth arguments are the output format and the resolution it's rasterized at,
defaulting to <code>jpg</code> at 300 DPI:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">150</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<ul>
<li>six formats are supported — <code>jpg</code>, <code>jpeg</code>, <code>png</code>, <code>webp</code>, <code>tiff</code> and <code>tif</code> — matched
case-insensitively, and the format sets the extension on every file written</li>
<li>resolution decides the pixel dimensions: a US Letter page comes out 2550 by 3300 pixels at the
default 300 DPI, 1275 by 1650 at 150</li>
<li>JPEG and WebP write at quality 90 rather than the encoder's own default, because the usual
destination for an extracted page is OCR, where compression artifacts along text edges cost more
than the bytes they save; PNG and TIFF are lossless already and are written as they come</li>
</ul>
<p>Reading a page's own size back is a matter of <code>getimagesize()</code> on the returned path:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>);

[<span class="text-var">$width</span>, <span class="text-var">$height</span>] = <span class="text-fn">getimagesize</span>(<span class="text-var">$images</span>[<span class="text-num">1</span>]);
<span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$width</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;x&#039;</span> . <span class="text-var">$height</span>;
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="naming-the-output-files">Naming the Output Files<a class="anchor" href="#naming-the-output-files" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>The fifth argument, <code>$filenameFormat</code>, is a <code>sprintf()</code> string that receives the source file's name
without its extension as argument 1 and the 1-based page number as argument 2; the extension is
appended afterward, so the format string covers the stem only. It defaults to <code>'%1$s-%2$02d'</code>,
which is where <code>invoice-01</code> comes from.</p>
<p>Dropping the stem gives files named for the page alone:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">filenameFormat</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;page-%2$02d&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That writes <code>page-01.png</code>, <code>page-02.png</code> and <code>page-03.png</code>. Changing the padding and separator
gives the unpadded form:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">filenameFormat</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;page_%2$d&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That writes <code>page_1.png</code>, <code>page_2.png</code> and <code>page_3.png</code>. Both positional references stay available
in any order and with any padding, so <code>'%1$s_page_%2$03d'</code> writes <code>invoice_page_001.png</code>.</p>
<h2 id="selecting-pages">Selecting Pages<a class="anchor" href="#selecting-pages" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>$pages</code> and <code>$pageLimit</code> are the last two arguments, and they sit behind <code>$filenameFormat</code>, so pass
them by name:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$firstTwo</span>    = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">pageLimit</span>: <span class="text-num">2</span>);
<span class="text-var">$oneAndThree</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: [<span class="text-num">1</span>, <span class="text-num">3</span>]);
</code></pre>
</div>

<ul>
<li><code>$pages</code> takes an array of 1-based page numbers, or a single number on its own — <code>pages: 2</code> and
<code>pages: [2]</code> mean the same thing; <code>$pageLimit</code> takes the first <em>n</em> pages of the document</li>
<li>an explicit <code>$pages</code> list wins outright: passing <code>pages: [3]</code> alongside <code>pageLimit: 1</code> writes
page 3, not page 1</li>
<li>filtering keeps the source document's numbering — <code>pages: [1, 3]</code> returns the keys <code>1</code> and <code>3</code>
and writes <code>invoice-01.png</code> and <code>invoice-03.png</code>, so a result key is always the page it came from,
whatever selection produced it; that's the opposite of
<a href="/extract/image-only#asking-page-by-page"><code>getImageOnlyPages()</code></a>, whose array is keyed from zero</li>
<li>a page number past the end of the document drops out of the selection, and a <code>$pageLimit</code> larger
than the document extracts every page, so the count of the result tells you how much of a
requested range the document actually held</li>
</ul>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$requested</span> = [<span class="text-num">1</span>, <span class="text-num">9</span>];
<span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: <span class="text-var">$requested</span>);

<span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-fn">count</span>(<span class="text-var">$images</span>) . <span class="text-str">&#039; of &#039;</span> . <span class="text-fn">count</span>(<span class="text-var">$requested</span>) . <span class="text-str">&#039; requested pages written&#039;</span>;
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="extracting-for-ocr">Extracting for OCR<a class="anchor" href="#extracting-for-ocr" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>Pdf::isImageOnlyDocument()</code> reports whether a document is scanned images rather than real text,
and gates this call naturally: when it returns <code>true</code>, the pages have to go through OCR instead of
text extraction.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$file</span> = <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>;

<span class="text-kw">if</span> (<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">isImageOnlyDocument</span>(<span class="text-var">$file</span>)) {
    <span class="text-kw">foreach</span> (<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-var">$file</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;png&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">resolution</span>: <span class="text-num">300</span>) <span class="text-kw">as</span> <span class="text-var">$pageNumber</span> =&gt; <span class="text-var">$image</span>) {
        <span class="text-comment">// hand $image to an OCR engine, attribute the result to $pageNumber</span>
    }
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Because the result is keyed by source page number, whatever an OCR engine returns can be attributed
straight back to the page it came from. See <a href="/extract/image-only">Image-Only Pages</a> for the
per-page classification behind that check.</p>
<h2 id="errors">Errors<a class="anchor" href="#errors" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Four conditions raise <code>Pop\Pdf\Build\Exception</code>, each one a thing to have in place before the call:</p>
<ul>
<li>Install the <code>imagick</code> extension, which is what does the rasterizing.</li>
<li>Pass a <code>$file</code> that exists on disk.</li>
<li>Pass a <code>$location</code> that is an existing, writable directory.</li>
<li>Pass one of the six supported formats.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each message names what it found:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Build\Exception</span>;

<span class="text-kw">try</span> {
    <span class="text-var">$images</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractAsImages</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/invoice.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/pages&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">format</span>: <span class="text-str">&#039;bmp&#039;</span>);
} <span class="text-kw">catch</span> (<span class="text-type">Exception</span> <span class="text-var">$e</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$e</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getMessage</span>();
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That prints <code>Error: The format 'bmp' is not supported.</code></p>
